# XCU expand
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Tests use single-column characters in the POSIX locale.

assertion  XCU.expand.001
anchor     utilities/expand.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/expand.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       By default expand replaces each tab by the spaces that reach the
           next tab stop, the stops being every eighth column; a tab at a
           stop goes to the following stop, and lines without tabs are
           unchanged.
test       t/001-default-stops.sh

assertion  XCU.expand.002
anchor     utilities/expand.html#OPTIONS/-t
class      required
since      1992
says       expand -t number puts the tab stops number columns apart.
test       t/002-tab-size.sh

assertion  XCU.expand.003
anchor     utilities/expand.html#OPTIONS/-t
class      required
since      1992
says       expand -t with a comma- or blank-separated list sets tabs at those
           columns, and a tab beyond the last one becomes a single space.
test       t/003-tab-list.sh

assertion  XCU.expand.004
anchor     utilities/expand.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       A backspace is copied to the output and lowers the column count
           that later tabs use.
test       t/004-backspace.sh

assertion  XCU.expand.005
anchor     utilities/expand.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/expand.html#CONSEQUENCES OF ERRORS
class      required
since      1992
says       expand handles file operands in order, reads standard input with no
           operand, and ends with a diagnostic and a nonzero status when a
           file cannot be accessed.
test       t/005-operands.sh
